## The short version

The **north** has more of the things expats look for on paper: more international schools, more private clinics and more developments approved for foreign buyers on the Economic Development Board's lists. The **west** is the driest and sunniest side of the island, faces the sunset, and has the national park, Le Morne and Chamarel on its doorstep.

## Weather

The whole island has warm, humid summers from November to April and cool, dry winters from June to September. The trade winds bring more rain to the east; the west coast, sheltered from them, is the driest and sunniest side.

## Schools

On the EDB's list of international schools, the west coast has four: Paul et Virginie and Telfair primary schools in Tamarin, and Westcoast International Primary (Cascavelle) and Secondary (Medine). The north has more, including Saint Exupéry International School in Grand Baie, Ecole du Nord and Northfields International High School in Mapou, Lighthouse schools in Calebasses and Greencoast International Schools at Beau Plan.

## Healthcare

The EDB lists two private clinics on our west coast (Clinique de l'Occident in Flic en Flac and Artemis Cascavelle Hospital) and three on the north coast (Clinique de Grand Baie, Centre Médical du Nord at Pointe aux Canonniers and a clinic at Trou aux Biches).

## Property

On the EDB's November 2022 list of Real Estate Scheme projects, 52 of the 77 are in the north and 22 on our west coast. Smart cities exist on both coasts: Cap Tamarin and Medine in the west, Beau Plan and Mon Choisy among those in the north. See [how buying works](/en/living-in-the-west/how-buying-works).

## Our verdict

Choose the north for the widest choice of schools, clinics and homes. Choose the west for sunshine, sunsets, the mountains and a smaller, quieter coast. Compare [Tamarin and Grand Baie](/en/living-in-the-west/tamarin-vs-grand-baie), or find [the best area on the west coast](/en/living-in-the-west/best-area-to-live-on-the-west-coast).

*Figures come from the official sources listed below, checked on 3 October 2026. Prices change: ask local agents, schools and your notary for current figures before you decide.*
